?For Whom to Produce?
This problem relates to the distribution of produced goods
and services among the individuals within the economy,
i.e. selection of the category of people who will ultimately
consume the goods. i.e. whether to produce goods for
more poor and iess rich r more rich and less poor.
It must be noted that production is the result of combined
efforts of factors of production. The output emerging from
production is distributed as factor income (rent, wages,
interest and profit) on the basis of their contribution in
production. So, the problem of 'For Whom to Produce' is
actually concerned with distribution of income.
